  [IS THE MASS REALLY DYNAMICAL?]  A transparent Wolf-style estimator 4 sigma_0^2 r_h/G
     built from the SAME table's central dispersion, compared with the N-body mass:
     median ratio 0.853, scatter 0.051 dex, N = 126
     d log(M_Wolf/M_Nbody)/d log B = -0.062 +- 0.025
     -> a ratio flat in B means the N-body masses ARE tracking the kinematics for the
        boosted clusters too, so the kill cannot be blamed on photometric masses.
  [PASS] the N-body masses do not drift systematically against a transparent kinematic estimator as the predicted boost grows (so the kill is not an artefact of photometric masses)  [CAN FAIL]   (slope -0.062 +- 0.025)

  [RANGE OF VALIDITY -- the most important caveat]  The clusters that carry the exclusion
     are the ones with a large predicted boost, and those all sit at LOW external field:
       B > 1.60 subset: e_ext = 0.004-0.407, R_GC = 14.4-147 kpc
     The frozen Gaia DR4 wide-binary prediction sits at e = 1.289 (the solar circle), where
     B = 1.34 and NO globular cluster is saturated (they are all internally denser than the
     local Galactic field).  So this kill excludes the SMALL-e end of B(e) and leaves the
     solar-neighbourhood end for December.  Saying otherwise would over-claim.

  [CONTROLLED REGRESSION, N = 126]  log10(M/L_V) ~ 1 + log B + MFSlope + log N_RV
     log B      -0.242 +- 0.066   (framework 1, Newton 0)
     MFSlope    -0.055 +- 0.018   (dynamical-evolution control)
     log N_RV   -0.028 +- 0.014   (measurement-quality control)

  [FOIL] log R_GC alone: slope -0.074 +- 0.021; r(log B, log M/L) = -0.216 vs r(log R_GC, log M/L) = -0.298
  [REDDENING FOIL] log10(M/L_V) on log|b|: slope -0.101 +- 0.023  (a large negative slope would mean the M/L_V column is not dereddened; un-dereddened light would INFLATE low-|b| = low-B clusters and bias the test AGAINST the law)
  [CONSPIRACY BUDGET] to hide the predicted contrast the true Upsilon_V of the boosted clusters would have to be 0.387 dex BELOW the unboosted ones.
     Metallicity does push that way -- outer-halo clusters are metal-poor and stellar
     populations give Upsilon_V ~ 2.0 at [Fe/H] = -0.5 and ~1.5 at -2.0, i.e. at most 0.12 dex.
     Shortfall that metallicity cannot cover: 0.267 dex.

