  UPSILON LEVER, numerically.
    The tested quantity is B_hat = (M/L_V)_dyn / Upsilon_V.  M/L_V is measured (dynamical mass over
    observed light) and carries NO stellar M/L assumption; Upsilon_V enters only as the denominator
    of the amplitude.  So:
      d log B_hat / d log Upsilon_V   =  -1.000  (exactly, by construction) -- the AMPLITUDE test
      d (slope of log M/L_V on log B) / d log Upsilon_V  =  0.000 -- the SHAPE test is Upsilon-free
    A 0.1 dex error in Upsilon_V moves the amplitude by 0.1 dex and the slope not at all.  The shape
    test is therefore the load-bearing one, and it is the one reported as the verdict.

RESULT: 8 checks, 0 FAIL   rc=0
